               steps: [
                   "Cook the rice however you always cook rice; in this meal it is the quiet center, not the performance.",
                   "Simmer the lentils with half the turmeric and 4 cups water until fully soft, 30 to 35 minutes, then whisk briefly so the dal turns loose and pourable, and salt it.",
                   "Heat a tablespoon of ghee until shimmering, sizzle half the cumin seeds and half the garlic to deep gold, and pour the sputtering tempering straight into the dal.",
                   "For the tarkari, fry the potatoes in the remaining ghee five minutes, add cauliflower, ginger, remaining cumin, turmeric, and salt, then cover and cook, stirring now and then, until tender and browned in spots, about 15 minutes.",
                   "Wilt the greens in the same pan with the remaining garlic and a pinch of salt, two to three minutes, just until they collapse but stay bright.",
                   "Build each steel plate, or regular plate, with rice in the center, dal poured generously over it, tarkari and greens beside, and a small fierce spoonful of pickle on the rim.",
                   "Offer seconds before anyone asks; in a Nepali kitchen the refill is not hospitality, it is the baseline.",
               ],
               note: "The dal should pour like heavy cream, never stand like porridge, and the tempering must audibly sizzle when it hits, or it was not hot enough.",
               shortcut: "Red lentils cook in half the time of black ones and make an honest weeknight dal; the flavor is lighter and less earthy."),
        Recipe(dishID: "nepal-momo", serves: 4, prepMinutes: 60, cookMinutes: 25, difficulty: 3,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "40", item: "round dumpling wrappers (gyoza wrappers work)"),
