                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 tbsp", item: "mustard oil (or vegetable oil plus 1 tsp yellow mustard)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "ground turmeric"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tsp", item: "chili powder"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1", item: "red onion, cut in thick rings"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2", item: "limes"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Cut the meat into generous 1 1/2-inch cubes, leaving the fat attached; on the Dharan highway the drip and flare is considered part of the recipe.",
                   "Work the ground Sichuan pepper, ginger, garlic, mustard oil, turmeric, chili powder, and salt into the meat with your hands until every piece is stained.",
                   "Marinate covered in the refrigerator at least four hours, and overnight if dinner can wait; the timur-style numbing note needs time to sink in.",
                   "Thread the cubes onto skewers, packed snugly so the meat stays juicy, and let them lose their fridge chill while the fire heats.",
                   "Grill over hot charcoal, or under a broiler set high with the meat close to the element, turning every few minutes, until charred outside and just cooked through, 10 to 12 minutes.",
                   "Rest the skewers five minutes, squeeze lime over everything, and serve with the raw onion rings and, if you can find it, a bowl of beaten rice.",
               ],
               note: "Wood or charcoal is the argument the whole dish makes; a gas grill works, but get real char on the corners or it is just kebab.",
               shortcut: "Chicken thighs take the same marinade, need only two hours, and cook faster; you trade the gamey depth that goat people prize."),
        Recipe(dishID: "nepal-chatamari", serves: 4, prepMinutes: 15, cookMinutes: 30, difficulty: 2,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/2 cups", item: "rice flour"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/4 cups", item: "water, more as needed"),
