               steps: [
                   "Whisk the rice flour with the water and half the salt into a batter the consistency of thin pancake batter; it should coat a spoon and run off in a stream.",
                   "Brown the ground meat in a teaspoon of oil with the ginger, garlic, cumin, chile, and remaining salt, breaking it fine, until cooked through and a little crisp at the edges.",
                   "Heat a lightly oiled nonstick skillet over medium, pour in a small ladle of batter, and swirl the pan at once into a thin 8-inch round.",
