                   "Cover and cook on medium-low until the base is set with a lacy browned underside and the egg is barely set, four to five minutes; a chatamari is never flipped.",
                   "Slide it out whole, repeat with the remaining batter and toppings, and cut each into wedges to share, hands only, the way a Newar feast would.",
               ],
               note: "Never flip it and never rush the covered stage; the lid steams the egg and topping while the rice base crisps underneath, which is the whole trick.",
               shortcut: "Call it Nepali pizza and a skeptical table will try it, though in Kathmandu that nickname costs you some goodwill."),
        Recipe(dishID: "nepal-selroti", serves: 6, prepMinutes: 25, cookMinutes: 30, difficulty: 2,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 cups", item: "rice flour"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1", item: "ripe banana, mashed smooth"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "sugar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tbsp", item: "ghee, melted (or butter)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 cup", item: "whole milk, more as needed"),
